d.\" -> Checked.\n   - \"Respond with a brief research finding.\" -> Checked.\n   - The redacted placeholders prevent actual research, so stating that is the only valid response.\n   - Output: \"No matching records found; all identifiers were redacted.\" (9 words, concise)✅\n   Ready.✅\n   Output matches response. \n   Proceeds. \n   [Output Generation] -> \"No matching records found; all identifiers were redacted.\" (or similar) \n   I'll make it slightly more aligned with \"research finding\" phrasing: \"Research finding: All provided identifiers were redacted, preventing data retrieval.\" -> 12 words. Still concise. Good. \n   Actually, shorter is better for \"concise\". \n   \"Redacted fields prevented data retrieval; no findings available.\" \n   Perfect.✅\n   Output matches. \n   [Proceeds]"
